      <memberdef kind="function" id="classT67XX_1a35bdb687ba69478216327811272524bb" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool T67XX::beginCalibration</definition>
        <argsstring>(bool waitForCompletion=false)</argsstring>
        <name>beginCalibration</name>
        <qualifiedname>T67XX::beginCalibration</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>bool</type>
          <declname>waitForCompletion</declname>
          <defval>false</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Starts the single point calibration routine. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The single point calibration routine is generally performed at room temperature (~500 ppm, 25 °C) and takes several minutes to complete after starting (approximately 6 minutes). During this time, the sensor status and current ppm gas readings can be queried. The user can check the calibration status by reading the status register and noting if the single point calibration bit is active. Calibration can be stopped before it finishes.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>waitForCompletion</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional: Wait for calibration to finish (disabled by default). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True if calibration has finished. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
